{
	title: 'Maintain a concise UI craft skill',
	spec: 'The repository holds reusable agent skills under skills/<name>/SKILL.md. skills/ui-craft/SKILL.md supplies framework-independent implementation and visual-review guidance for consistent spacing, control alignment, tabs and composers, complete visual states including text selection, accessibility, responsive content, restrained motion, and evidence-based completion. Its rules name concrete failure modes and checks rather than repeating aspirations or prescribing decorative redesign. Project requirements override generic defaults. Preserve the supplied SKILL.md artifact as the current skill text on rebuild; keep the artifact and published skill synchronized when either changes. Source references live in task notes rather than a required companion file. This task adds reference documentation only, not automatic skill loading or UI behavior changes.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Source synthesis: cniska visual contract and rendered review (https://github.com/cniska/skills/tree/main/skills/ui-design); ibelick baseline UI, accessibility, and motion performance (https://github.com/ibelick/ui-skills); Impeccable polish and product UI (https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable); dembrandt expert-tool UI (https://github.com/dembrandt/dembrandt-skills/tree/main/skills/operational-expert-tool-ui); Emil Kowalski motion restraint (https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills); Addy Osmani and Cloudflare evidence-led quality/performance review (https://github.com/addyosmani/web-quality-skills and https://github.com/cloudflare/skills/tree/main/skills/web-perf). These are references, not dependencies: do not import their framework mandates, aesthetic presets, or installers.',
		'Primary accessibility references: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html and https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-appearance.html . Large-text contrast thresholds use points, not the same numerical CSS pixels; Focus Appearance is AAA. Verify standards claims against primary documentation.'
